e\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"049d498f7029431cee46edfc92c77d78d5617bf82a847fb70a676b6a2e93d3f7","event_uuid":"715621e6-a59c-4bab-ba4f-0a7a0624ee0b","position":{"commit_sha":"88478cd82d2790ae1fe14bfc46f29cc99e9d4575","position":"1787916641485497001-715621e6-a59c-4bab-ba4f-0a7a0624ee0b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"222493cb54c1933bf21df1d08d587c2a32c0bc4dfe81b9f011696e890f100276","event_uuid":"3be816f7-3a2f-442b-a9f5-1df5dd3866ae","position":{"commit_sha":"6cdffc420a2996d08b8c24d7ae61de6f3a147844","position":"1787917132774726001-3be816f7-3a2f-442b-a9f5-1df5dd3866ae"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ca0154f79baa00bd6f51e7a3348a93655a352134db248fda9043893c56fd8bb3","event_uuid":"8e7ff2e5-fc8d-4f63-8b46-db20700c8264","position":{"commit_sha":"edab3f345476c48097081a7bf67f14b4de4868a2","position":"1787917142028486001-8e7ff2e5-fc8d-4f63-8b46-db20700c8264"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787866195650114468,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"862764f6-ee27-48b3-b22c-004611a57f4f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"524d-22a5-1a21-49d7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nrebar stamps the claiming coding-agent session onto a ticket's `open -> in_progress`\nclaim edge (`claimed_session`, plus `claim_harness` / `claim_remote_session`) — see\n`docs/event-schema.md` §\"Session provenance (`claimed_session`)\" and the reducer fold\n`_fold_claimed_session` (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors_status.py:25`). Because `claim`\nis a *soft* lock and events merge as a union (`docs/concurrency.md`), a second agent\n**session** can freely operate on a ticket a first session is actively working —\ncomment, edit, tag, transition, or even just `show` it. Parallel agents commonly run\nunder the **same assignee** but **different session ids**, so assignee cannot\ndistinguish them. Today there is no signal when session B touches a ticket session A\nholds `in_progress`, so B can unknowingly step onto A's in-flight work.\n\nThis epic adds a **non-blocking warning** surfaced on all three surfaces (CLI, MCP,\nlibrary) whenever an operation that targets **one specific ticket** is performed by a\nsession different from the one that currently holds the ticket `in_progress`. It also\ntightens ownership semantics so \"held\" means exactly \"currently `in_progress` by\nsession X\": the claim-session provenance is **cleared on every exit from\n`in_progress`**.\n\nDeliberate design decisions (settled during brainstorm):\n- Ownership is by **session id** (`claimed_session`), never assignee.\n- **Warn, do not block** — the permissive event-union model is unchanged.\n- Fires **only on single-ticket-targeted operations** (single-ticket reads like `show`\n  plus single-ticket mutations); **bulk reads never warn** (`list` / `search` /\n  `ready` / `next-batch`), because those exist precisely to hand parallel agents *other*\n  tickets and would emit a wall of warnings.\n- **Silent when the acting session id is unknown** (`resolve_session_id()` is `None` —\n  the common un-shimmed case), documented as an **evidence-revisitable** choice.\n- Gated by a **config toggle**, default **on**.\n- Accepted known limitation: a session id is not stable across `--resume` / fork /\n  subagents (`docs/session-id-shims.md` gotcha G1), so the same agent can present a new\n  id and warn about \"its own\" ticket; the toggle is the escape hatch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `claimed_session`, `claim_harness`, and `claim_remote_session` are cleared on\n  every `in_progress -> {open,blocked,closed,idea}` transition, so a non-`in_progress`\n  ticket never reports a stale holder — delivered by the reducer-clearing story;\n  proxy: its reducer tests assert the cleared state.\n- [x] A single shared detector decides when to warn — warns exactly when the toggle is\n  on, the acting session id is known, and it differs from a *live* `claimed_session`;\n  silent otherwise — delivered by the detector+config story; proxy: its unit matrix\n  passes.\n- [x] The warning is surfaced for single-ticket-targeted operations on **CLI** (stderr\n  line), **MCP** (structured response field), and **library** (`warnings.warn`), and\n  never on bulk reads — delivered by the three per-surface stories; proxy: each\n  surface's tests assert warn-on-mismatch and silence on same-session / bulk / unset-id.\n\n## Child decomposition\n\n- **Reducer clearing** — clear the three claim-session fields on every exit from\n  `in_progress` (reducer + `docs/event-schema.md`). Foundation for \"live holder\"\n  semantics; every other child depends on it.\n- **Detector + config toggle** — the pure `cross_session_warning` helper and the\n  `warnings.cross_session` config key (default true), plus `docs/config-reference.md`.\n  Depends on reducer clearing.\n- **CLI surface** — emit a `WARN:` stderr line for single-ticket CLI commands. Depends\n  on the detector.\n- **MCP surface** — carry the warning in single-ticket MCP tool responses (mirroring\n  the existing `description_warning` field). Depends on the detector.\n- **Library surface** — `warnings.warn` a dedicated warning category from single-ticket\n  library functions. Depends on the detector.\n\nEach child owns a distinct, non-overlapping seam (reducer state, pure detector+config,\nCLI rendering, MCP model/schema, library warnings channel).","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_reopened_at":1787914485102143001,"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","524d-22a5-1a21-49d7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"3be816f7-3a2f-442b-a9f5-1df5dd3866ae","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"1aca-695f-a0a4-4236","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Cross-session operation warning + clear claim-session on exit from in_progress","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1026cd7f-6d68-4b83-b730-2e855066c3d2","9203deee-ac66-459a-8595-367e00a76b9c","354206a4-5d75-44e6-b3ff-fcd8727324a3","487d0811-314a-487a-8c0a-976a68e5b7d1","861eaa54-e44e-447a-9c41-81737d6ae87f","71001095-b5d8-4bd9-8592-73c0bb9fd99e","563bf548-cca2-416c-b2f4-2e2e2aa6ad19","05af9cde-2cdf-4e07-846c-14264c5552cf","eb136338-39fa-4d1f-b13e-6b0a6e650939","287126c7-fda1-4c64-b14d-0be8d0cdf06d","1735c060-8844-4e14-b64e-ea4df959b07f","715621e6-a59c-4bab-ba4f-0a7a0624ee0b","3be816f7-3a2f-442b-a9f5-1df5dd3866ae","8e7ff2e5-fc8d-4f63-8b46-db20700c8264"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787933535737283337,"uuid":"eaabaa38-8187-4a62-9b70-ad895a6df863"}